sieve-filter-v2
; The first and last samples within `quiet` percent of full scale of silence, so a sound begins and
; ends as recorded sound in a clip does (from and to quiet) rather than cut in the middle of a wave.
; The samples between are free.
id        pcm-quiet-ends
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   pcm*
describe  The first and last samples near silence (within quiet percent of full scale).
param     quiet  int  5  0  100  how near silence the first and last samples must be, in percent of full scale

; State 0: the start (the first sample must be quiet). State 1: the last sample was quiet. State 2:
; it was not.
states    3
start     0
accept    1
for d 0 {BASE - 1}
  if {abs(d - BASE * (d >= BASE / 2)) * 100 <= quiet * (BASE / 2)}
    t 0 @{d} 1
    t 1 @{d} 1
    t 2 @{d} 1
  else
    t 1 @{d} 2
    t 2 @{d} 2
  fi
done
end
